WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:01.775
- [Voiceover] It's Hamburg, Germany.

00:00:01.775 --> 00:00:03.192
The year is 1669.

00:00:04.761 --> 00:00:07.857
Inside of a basement laboratory,
alchemist Hennig Brand

00:00:07.857 --> 00:00:09.462
is boiling gallons of urine

00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:12.397
to create the fabled philosopher's stone.

00:00:12.397 --> 00:00:14.077
Unbeknownst to him, the urine

00:00:14.077 --> 00:00:17.448
is about to lead to a truly
world-altering discovery.

00:00:17.448 --> 00:00:19.547
(inquisitive grumble)
(lively music)

00:00:19.547 --> 00:00:21.414
During the middle ages,
the philosopher's stone

00:00:21.414 --> 00:00:23.988
was the coveted discovery
because it was believed

00:00:23.988 --> 00:00:26.416
it could turn ordinary metal to gold.

00:00:26.416 --> 00:00:28.880
In his quest to find it, Brand accumulated

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.237
over 1,500 gallons of urine.

00:00:31.237 --> 00:00:32.289
(chuckling)

00:00:32.289 --> 00:00:34.476
He thought that by purifying the waste

00:00:34.476 --> 00:00:37.876
the philosopher's stone would
materialize in what was left.

00:00:37.876 --> 00:00:39.651
The process went like this.

00:00:39.651 --> 00:00:41.547
One, age the urine until

00:00:41.547 --> 00:00:44.377
an intense odor billows
out of the samples.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:48.791
Two, boil the urine until
a white paste materializes.

00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:52.181
Three, place the heated
paste in a retort.

00:00:52.181 --> 00:00:54.774
Four, gold will then drip out of the—

00:00:54.774 --> 00:00:55.607
(inquisitive grumble)

00:00:55.607 --> 00:00:56.876
Wait what?

00:00:56.876 --> 00:00:57.709
(chiming bell)

00:00:57.709 --> 00:01:00.014
Okay, so it wasn't gold that emerged,

00:01:00.014 --> 00:01:03.057
but a solid white substance
that glowed in the dark.

00:01:03.057 --> 00:01:06.050
This was big, this was bigger than big.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.729
His discovery was gonna change the world.

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:10.625
Brand had discovered phosphorus

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:12.689
one of the building blocks of life.

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.039
Making him the first person

00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:16.587
to ever discover a chemical element,

00:01:16.587 --> 00:01:19.009
but the thing was, he had no idea.

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:21.649
He believed he had found a
glowing philosopher's stone

00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:23.907
and named the substance phosphorus,

00:01:23.907 --> 00:01:26.004
meaning bringer of light.

00:01:26.004 --> 00:01:28.040
Brand kept his discovery a secret

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.074
until he eventually sold his
process to other scientists.

00:01:32.074 --> 00:01:33.919
It wasn't until after his death

00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:37.009
that he was given credit
for discovering phosphorus.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:40.273
All by boiling urine in
his basement laboratory.

00:01:40.273 --> 00:01:44.106
(dramatic instrumental music)

